import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.DSMap.Mix2
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.Basic
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.PerfComplexDefs
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.H0Defs
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.cechIso
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.rootKillingFromZeroRoot
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.orbitKill
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.orbitUniform

namespace Work.DSM5b

open CategoryTheory DSMap DSMap.Mix DSMap.Mix2
universe a

/-- **M5b in positive degrees** (the heart of the node): multiplication by the `p`-power root
`ϖ k = T ^ (1/p^k)` of `T` kills the positive-degree cohomology of the perfected chart Čech complex
`K = (cechComplexFunctor (chartIdx ι)).obj (perfChartPresheaf p t)` of the blowup of `Spec R` along
`J = (t_i)` (`R` perfect of characteristic `p`, `t j₀ = T ^ e`).

## The route implemented here (and the *fusion* of the two halves of the node)

**Step 1 (localisation/descent = power killing).**  Invert `T`.  Since `t j₀ = T ^ e` the ideal
`J = (t_i)` becomes the unit ideal, the localised chart rings become `R[1/(T t_S)]`, and the
localised complex is the Amitsur complex of the covering family `{D(t_i)}` of `Spec R[1/T]`, hence
exact in positive degrees with `H⁰ = R[1/T]`; clearing denominators gives *power killing*: every
cycle `w` of the honest chart complex `HCX t ·` satisfies `T ^ N w = d y` for some `N`.  This is
`Work.DSM5b.honestPowerKilling` (sorry-free), and it holds over *any* commutative ring.

**Step 2 (the `φ`-orbit criterion) — the correct replacement of the DESIGN's invalid "Frobenius
upgrade".**  The perfected chart rings are perfect (`Work.DSM5b.perfChartRing_pow_p_mem_iff`), so
the componentwise `p`-th power map `φ` is a bijection of the perfected complex `PCX p t ·` commuting
with the differentials and `R`-semilinear (`φ (r x) = r ^ p • φ x`); write `ψ = φ⁻¹`, with
`ψ (r x) = r ^ (1/p) • ψ x`.  The DESIGN's Step 2 (upgrade a *single* relation `(ϖ k) ^ m z = d y`
to `ϖ k • z = d y`) is **false**: the `ψ`/`φ` moves are information free on a single relation
(abstract counterexample: `M = R_T / R`, `R = 𝔽_p[T^(1/p^∞)]`, `x = 1/T²`, `d = 0`, where
`ϖ k ^ m x = 0` for `m ≫ 0` but `ϖ k x ≠ 0`).  What *is* true (and is what the geometry supplies)
is the *uniformity along the whole `φ`-orbit of the cycle*: if one exponent `N` kills **all** the
`φ ^ E z` at once, then `T • z ∈ range (PCd p t n)`.  Indeed, given `p ^ E ≥ N`, applying `ψ ^ E`
to `T ^ N • φ ^ E z = d y` produces `(T ^ (1/p^E)) ^ N • z = d (ψ ^ E y)`, and multiplying by the
complementary power `(T ^ (1/p^E)) ^ (p^E - N) ∈ R` gives `T • z = d (…)`.  This is
`Work.DSM5b.orbitKill_of_uniformOrbit` (proved in `Submission/Work/DSM5b/orbitKill.lean`).

**Step 2′ (the uniform orbit bound).**  The needed input `∃ N, ∀ E, T ^ N • φ ^ E z ∈ range (PCd)`
is `Work.DSM5b.orbitUniform` (`Submission/Work/DSM5b/orbitUniform.lean`).  Its proof is *support +
Noetherian*: the cycle `z` has finitely many components, each a finite polynomial expression in
finitely many elements of `R`, so `z` lies in the subcomplex generated by a *finitely generated*
(hence Noetherian) subring `R₀ ⊆ R`; over `R₀` the Noetherian uniform honest killing
(`Work.DSM5b.honestKillCoordNoeth`, one exponent killing every honest cycle) applies to all the
honest elements `φ ^ E z` (`E ≫ 0`), and the elementary monotonicity
`killExp u ≤ killExp (φ u)` (`Work.DSM5b.killExp_le_killExp_phi`) pushes the finitely many
remaining levels up.  **Note that the uniform-over-`R` statement
`Work.DSM5b.honestKillCoord` is not needed (and is presumably false for general perfect `R`: it
fails for products of cones of unbounded degree); only the Noetherian case is.**

**Step 3 (levels).**  `k = 0` (multiplier `T`) implies every level `k`: `φ ^ k (ϖ k • y) = T • φ ^ k y`
and `φ ^ k` is a bijection of each perfected chart ring — this is
`Work.DSM5b.rootKillingFromZeroRoot` (sorry-free), so it suffices to prove the statement for
`k = 0`, which is step 2.

**Step 4 (coordinates).**  The same statement in the coordinates `PCX`/`PCd` of the complex, and
transported along the chain isomorphism `Work.DSM5b.cechIso` (sorry-free, proved).

Do NOT use the frozen sorried declaration `DSMap.Mix2.area_M5b`; the proof comes from the
definitions. -/
theorem perfectedRootKilling (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (R : Type a) [CommRing R] [CharP R p]
    [PerfectRing R p] {ι : Type a} [Finite ι] [DecidableEq ι] (t : ι → R) (T : R) (j₀ : ι) (e : ℕ)
    (hj₀ : t j₀ = T ^ e) (k : ℕ) :
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (z : ((cechComplexFunctor (chartIdx ι)).obj (perfChartPresheaf p t)).X (n + 1)),
      ((cechComplexFunctor (chartIdx ι)).obj (perfChartPresheaf p t)).d (n + 1) (n + 2) z = 0 →
      ∃ y : ((cechComplexFunctor (chartIdx ι)).obj (perfChartPresheaf p t)).X n,
        (frobeniusEquiv R p).symm^[k] T • z =
          ((cechComplexFunctor (chartIdx ι)).obj (perfChartPresheaf p t)).d n (n + 1) y := by
  intro n z hz
  obtain ⟨ee, hee⟩ := _root_.Work.DSM5b.Work.DSM5b.cechIso p t
  -- root killing on the coordinate complex `PCX p t ·`
  have hzy : PCd p t (n + 1) ((ee (n + 1)).hom z) = 0 := by
    have h := hee (n + 1) z
    rw [hz] at h
    simpa using h.symm
  obtain ⟨y', hy'⟩ := pcxRootKilling_of_orbit p t T j₀ e hj₀ (orbitUniform p t T j₀ e hj₀)
    k n ((ee (n + 1)).hom z) hzy
  refine ⟨(ee n).inv y', ?_⟩
  -- transport the relation back along the chain isomorphism
  have key : (ee (n + 1)).hom
      (((cechComplexFunctor (chartIdx ι)).obj (perfChartPresheaf p t)).d n (n + 1)
        ((ee n).inv y'))
      = (ee (n + 1)).hom (((frobeniusEquiv R p).symm^[k] T) • z) := by
    rw [hee n ((ee n).inv y')]
    simp only [ModuleCat.hom_ofHom]
    rw [show (ee n).hom ((ee n).inv y') = y' from (ee n).inv_hom_id_apply y', map_smul, hy']
  exact (ee (n + 1)).toLinearEquiv.injective key.symm

end Work.DSM5b
